E_ACME_DNS_TEST_FAILED	503	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ACME_DNS_TEST_FAILED	the DNS provider probe failed (create -> delete a real TXT record at _acme-challenge-test.<base_domain>; the failed step and the underlying provider error travel in the envelope context)	Fix the provider credentials per the failed probe step (create=auth/write incl. zone resolution, delete=cleanup) and test again; the honest contract is: test passed = the provider credentials can authenticate, write and delete TXT records under the platform domain.
E_ACME_WILDCARD_REQUIRES_BASE_DOMAIN	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ACME_WILDCARD_REQUIRES_BASE_DOMAIN	acme.wildcard=true requires a platform base domain (the wildcard domain set *.base with console/ctrl/registry.<base> derives from it)	Configure base_domain (installer --base-domain) before switching the wildcard on; the wildcard certificate covers every platform subdomain and app domain under it.
E_ACME_WILDCARD_REQUIRES_PROVIDER	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ACME_WILDCARD_REQUIRES_PROVIDER	acme.wildcard=true requires a DNS provider (dnspod or cloudflare): a wildcard SAN can only be validated via a DNS-01 challenge	Configure the DNS provider credentials first ('fleetly acme dns set --provider dnspod --token …' or the Console ACME card), then switch the wildcard on ('fleetly acme wildcard on').
E_ALERTS_METRICS_REQUIRED	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ALERTS_METRICS_REQUIRED	alerts.mode=on requires metrics.mode=on first (vmalert has no datasource without the managed VictoriaMetrics)	Enable the metrics stack first ('fleetly metrics mode set on' or the Console metrics card), wait for the three managed services to converge, then switch alerts on ('fleetly alerts mode on').
E_ALERT_RULE_CHANNELS_INVALID	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ALERT_RULE_CHANNELS_INVALID	an alert rule channels list is invalid (must be a list of non-empty notification endpoint ids; an empty list means deliver to all enabled endpoints)	List the notification endpoints with 'fleetly notifications endpoint list' and pass their ids (comma-separated on the CLI); leave it empty to fan out to every enabled endpoint.
E_ALERT_RULE_EXPR_INVALID	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ALERT_RULE_EXPR_INVALID	an alert rule expr is invalid (must be a non-empty PromQL expression of at most 2048 chars)	Write the PromQL condition that should evaluate to a series when the alert should fire (e.g. 'up == 0'); syntax is validated by vmalert/VictoriaMetrics — use 'fleetly alerts rules test' to evaluate it before saving.
E_ALERT_RULE_FOR_INVALID	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ALERT_RULE_FOR_INVALID	an alert rule for_duration is invalid (must be >= 0 seconds; 0 = no for clause)	Pass a non-negative number of seconds (e.g. --for 300 for a five-minute sustained condition before firing).
E_ALERT_RULE_LABELS_INVALID	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ALERT_RULE_LABELS_INVALID	an alert rule labels object is invalid (keys must be non-empty; values are strings; the severity label drives the notification text)	Provide a JSON object of string to string, e.g. {"severity":"critical"}; an empty object is valid.
E_ALERT_RULE_NAME_CONFLICT	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ALERT_RULE_NAME_CONFLICT	an alert rule with the same name already exists (rule names are unique platform-wide — alerting is a platform-admin domain)	Pick another rule name (or delete the old rule first); names are the operator-facing handle used by the CLI and Console.
E_ALERT_RULE_NOT_FOUND	404	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ALERT_RULE_NOT_FOUND	the alert rule referenced by the operation does not exist (or was already deleted)	List the rules with 'fleetly alerts rules ls' and retry with an existing id or name.
E_APP_AMBIGUOUS	400	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_APP_AMBIGUOUS	the resource name matches more than one row across projects (app/database names are unique per project, D-W0-4); bare-name references must be unique in the resolution scope	Qualify the reference as team/project/<name> or reference the resource by its platform id; e2e/CLI fixtures should avoid same-named resources until the qualified read face lands (S4).
E_APP_PROJECT_MISMATCH	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_APP_PROJECT_MISMATCH	the request targets a different project than the one the app row already belongs to (ownership on the row wins once assigned)	Deploy without the project field (it resolves to the row's own project) or move the app first: a platform administrator can reassign ownership with MoveApp (rename redeploy).
E_APP_PROJECT_REQUIRED	400	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_APP_PROJECT_REQUIRED	the pushed app does not exist yet and no project ownership can be derived from the push (no signed user or no default project)	Deploy once via CLI/API passing project "team/project" to create the app with ownership, then push; subsequent pushes deploy to the row's own project.
E_BACKUP_KEY_MISSING	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_BACKUP_KEY_MISSING	restore verification failed: checksum/master key fingerprint mismatch; half-restored state is rejected	Provide the correct backup set and master key; the restore flow rejects half-restored state — do not hand-assemble state.
E_BUILD_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_BUILD_FAILED	build stage failed (Railpack/BuildKit)	Check the build logs to locate the compile/dependency error, fix it, and deploy again.
E_CAPABILITY_REQUIRES_MULTI_NODE	400	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_CAPABILITY_REQUIRES_MULTI_NODE	multi-node operations are unavailable on the current topology or configuration (retired guard path; the code is retained and never reused)	This operation requires a multi-node topology with the platform base domain configured; multi-node support ships with v0.2 (see the join guide: fleetly nodes join-guide).
E_COMPOSE_MANAGED_FIELD	400	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_COMPOSE_MANAGED_FIELD	compose managed-field value violates platform governance (failure_action/monitor)	Set deploy.update_config.failure_action to pause (or omit it) and monitor to 5s (or omit it), then retry.
E_COMPOSE_UNSAFE_STRATEGY	400	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_COMPOSE_UNSAFE_STRATEGY	explicit start-first conflicts with platform-enforced stop-first (volumes/fixed host ports/global)	Set deploy.update_config.order to start-first or omit it; services with volumes or fixed host ports are forced to stop-first by the platform.
E_COMPOSE_UNSUPPORTED	400	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_COMPOSE_UNSUPPORTED	compose declaration falls outside the controlled subset/deny list; validation rejects it explicitly	Remove or rewrite the unsupported compose fields and retry; see the error code docs for the controlled subset and deny list.
E_CONFIG_NOT_FOUND	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_CONFIG_NOT_FOUND	a compose-declared external config is not in the platform config store (deploy preflight)	Create the config first (fleetly configs set) with the exact declared name, then deploy again; compose configs must declare external: true.
E_DB_BACKUP_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DB_BACKUP_FAILED	database backup job failed (resource-terminal class; surfaced primarily in the backup ledger and events)	Check the db_backups ledger error column and the db.backup_failed event for the failure summary; fix the cause and trigger the backup again.
E_DB_ENV_PREFIX_CONFLICT	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DB_ENV_PREFIX_CONFLICT	two databases referenced by the same app derive the same env prefix (e.g. pg-prod vs pg_prod)	Rename one of the database instances (or reference only one per colliding pair in this app): env prefixes are derived from instance names by uppercasing with '-' mapped to '_'.
E_DB_NOT_FOUND	404	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DB_NOT_FOUND	the referenced/operated database instance does not exist or has entered deleting/deleted (candidate list attached)	Check the database instance name against the database list; references are validated for existence only (not readiness — a not-ready database yields a plan warning instead).
E_DB_PROJECT_MISMATCH	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DB_PROJECT_MISMATCH	the referenced database instance belongs to a different project than the app (project isolation, R6/R7): cross-project database attachment is rejected at deploy admission	Move the database into the app's project first (a platform administrator can reassign it with MoveDatabase), or reference an instance created in the same project; the app's project is listed in the error context.
E_DB_REFERENCED	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DB_REFERENCED	database deletion refused while app references exist (reference list attached; data-safety sentinel)	Remove the fleetly.databases labels from the referencing apps and redeploy them first (the reference list in the error context names every blocking app/service).
E_DB_RESTORE_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DB_RESTORE_FAILED	database restore failed (an interrupted in-place restore is a critical alert, not a retry-quietly path)	Follow the restore runbook: verify the instance state and volume data, then re-run the restore from the same snapshot after fixing the cause.
E_DB_ROTATE_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DB_ROTATE_FAILED	credential rotation failed mid-flight (the completed stages are attached; manual completion may be required)	Check the attached completed stages and the instance state, finish the remaining stage manually or retry the rotation, then verify the referencing apps redeploy.
E_DB_TEMPLATE_UNSUPPORTED	400	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DB_TEMPLATE_UNSUPPORTED	unknown template id or a settings change violates the template-managed surface (image/engine parameters are not user-editable)	Use one of the built-in template ids (postgres-16, postgres-18, percona-postgresql-18, redis-7, mysql-8.4, mongodb-8.0) and limit settings changes to resource limits and the backup plan.
E_DEPLOY_CONFIRM_REQUIRED	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DEPLOY_CONFIRM_REQUIRED	deploy contains destructive changes (service removal/volume unbind) without the confirmation flag; rejected from queueing	This deploy will remove services or unbind volumes relative to the latest revision: confirm the intent and retry with --confirm-destructive.
E_DEPLOY_DOWNTIME_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DEPLOY_DOWNTIME_FAILED	stop-first downtime switch failed and forced recovery failed (permanent outage risk path)	Fix the start failure and deploy again; this path forces recovery and cannot roll back.
E_DEPLOY_INTERRUPTED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DEPLOY_INTERRUPTED	deploy interrupted (control plane stopped/node failure), state machine not completed	Start a new deploy to recover; if the traffic switch had not happened yet, traffic was unaffected.
E_DEPLOY_POST_WINDOW_UNSTABLE	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DEPLOY_POST_WINDOW_UNSTABLE	unstable verdict after the observe window passed (platform only alerts, no automatic rollback)	Check app logs to assess the impact; manual rollback is advised (no automatic rollback after the observe window).
E_DOMAIN_CONFLICT	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DOMAIN_CONFLICT	the same domain appears on two services of the same app	The domain is already claimed by another service of this app: remove it from one of them before declaring it.
E_DOMAIN_UNSUPPORTED	400	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_DOMAIN_UNSUPPORTED	domain form unsupported (e.g. wildcards require DNS-01 from v0.2)	Use a concrete domain; see the error code docs for wildcard and certificate support scope.
E_ENV_KEY_RESERVED	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ENV_KEY_RESERVED	user wrote into the reserved FLEETLY_ env namespace (template connection-string materialization keys)	FLEETLY_* env keys are platform-reserved (database connection materialization): rename the key without the FLEETLY_ prefix; system-source platform writes are unaffected.
E_EVENT_CURSOR_EXPIRED	410	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_EVENT_CURSOR_EXPIRED	event cursor predates the retention window (30 days); explicit gap	Re-fetch all events starting from the oldest_seq in the response.
E_HEALTH_TIMEOUT	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_HEALTH_TIMEOUT	health gate timeout: new task did not pass healthcheck within budget	Verify the healthcheck command and port are correct and the app can pass the health check within budget.
E_IMAGE_PULL_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_IMAGE_PULL_FAILED	image pull failed (registry unreachable/invalid credentials/network failure)	Verify the image reference and registry credentials are valid and the node can reach the registry, then retry.
E_IMAGE_UNAVAILABLE	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_IMAGE_UNAVAILABLE	rollback target image is no longer available (digest stale/pruned)	The rollback target image is no longer available: replay the most recent usable revision instead, or rebuild and deploy.
E_INIT_JOB_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_INIT_JOB_FAILED	release-time init job failed (task failed/rejected/shut down): the deployment fails before the new revision is promoted	Check the init job logs (attributed to the declaring compose service) to locate the failure, fix the job, and deploy again; completed jobs are not rolled back (migrations are forward-only).
E_INIT_JOB_TIMED_OUT	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_INIT_JOB_TIMED_OUT	release-time init job exceeded its watchdog budget (default 10m, fleetly.job.timeout label overrides): the deployment fails before promotion	Raise fleetly.job.timeout on the init service (a positive Go duration such as 30m) or speed up the migration, then deploy again.
E_INVITE_INVALID	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_INVITE_INVALID	the invite token is invalid, already used, revoked, or expired (one-time credential; the specific state is not disclosed)	Ask the team owner or admin for a fresh invite link; invite links are valid for 7 days and can be used exactly once.
E_LABEL_RESERVED	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_LABEL_RESERVED	user occupied the reserved namespace fleetly.*	fleetly.* is a platform-reserved namespace: use a different label prefix.
E_LOGS_BACKEND_UNAVAILABLE	503	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_LOGS_BACKEND_UNAVAILABLE	the unified log search face is unavailable (logs.backend=jsonl has no search face, or VictoriaLogs did not answer; live log tail is unaffected)	Check the current backend with 'fleetly logs backend show'. If it is jsonl, switch to victorialogs to enable search; if VictoriaLogs is unreachable, check the fleetly-victorialogs service — search recovers automatically once it answers (the degradation streak and dropped counter are surfaced in the same view).
E_METRICS_BACKEND_UNAVAILABLE	503	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_METRICS_BACKEND_UNAVAILABLE	the metrics query face is unavailable (VictoriaMetrics did not answer on the loopback face; the scrape face is unaffected)	Check the managed services with 'fleetly metrics status'. If the stack is still converging, wait for the services to appear; if VictoriaMetrics is running, verify the 127.0.0.1 loopback probe — the query face recovers automatically once it answers.
E_METRICS_NOT_ENABLED	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_METRICS_NOT_ENABLED	metrics collection is not enabled (metrics.mode=unset): the query face is opt-in and has nothing to report	Enable the metrics stack with 'fleetly metrics mode set on' (or the Console metrics card). Once the three managed services converge, SearchMetrics starts serving; the data volume survives disabling, so history resumes from where it stopped.
E_MULTI_NODE_REQUIRES_BASE_DOMAIN	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_MULTI_NODE_REQUIRES_BASE_DOMAIN	multi-node is not enabled: the platform base domain is not configured (join face refuses instead of silently degrading)	Configure base_domain (installer --base-domain) before joining nodes: the config endpoint (8423 TLS), platform subdomains and the zot registry all derive from it.
E_OBSERVE_CRASH_LOOP	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_OBSERVE_CRASH_LOOP	observe window verdict: crash loop	The process exited repeatedly during the observe window: check app logs to locate the crash cause and roll back manually if needed.
E_OBSERVE_UNHEALTHY	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_OBSERVE_UNHEALTHY	observe window verdict: unstable (never reached healthy)	The health verdict failed during the observe window: check app logs and health endpoints, and roll back manually if needed.
E_PLACEMENT_LABEL_CONFLICT	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_PLACEMENT_LABEL_CONFLICT	placement labels of multiple services in one app point to different nodes	Set fleetly.placement.node to the same node for all services of the app.
E_PLACEMENT_MOVE_REQUIRES_ACK	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_PLACEMENT_MOVE_REQUIRES_ACK	cross-node placement moves require explicit confirmation (data disposition and/or destructive-confirm missing)	A cross-node move is only valid with an explicit data disposition: --data-restored after the restore flow, or --discard with --confirm-destructive (admin+confirm+audited).
E_PLACEMENT_NODE_GONE	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_PLACEMENT_NODE_GONE	bound node was removed (blocked(node_gone)); in-flight deploys fail with this code	rebind --data-restored after data recovery, or rebind --discard after confirming discard (admin+confirm+audited).
E_PLACEMENT_NODE_INVALID	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_PLACEMENT_NODE_INVALID	failed to resolve node name/ID in the placement label (422 + candidate list)	Check the fleetly.placement.node value (a node name or platform node ID); see context for the candidate node list.
E_PLACEMENT_NODE_NOT_FOUND	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_PLACEMENT_NODE_NOT_FOUND	node referenced by the placement label does not exist or was removed	Pick a valid node from the node list and retry.
E_PLACEMENT_NODE_UNAVAILABLE	503	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_PLACEMENT_NODE_UNAVAILABLE	bound node is currently not ready (deploy preflight fails fast, no queueing)	Wait for the bound node to become ready, or change the binding via rebind after confirming data safety.
E_PLACEMENT_NO_ELIGIBLE_NODE	503	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_PLACEMENT_NO_ELIGIBLE_NODE	no candidate for automatic placement (no ready node satisfies the constraints)	Check node readiness and placement constraints; retry after a candidate node recovers.
E_PROJECT_AMBIGUOUS	400	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_PROJECT_AMBIGUOUS	the bare project name matches more than one visible project (same-name projects across teams are legal, D-W0-9)	Qualify the reference as team/project (e.g. acme/prod) and retry; the matching candidates are listed in the error context.
E_REGISTRATION_CLOSED	403	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_REGISTRATION_CLOSED	self-service registration is closed (auth.registration defaults to closed once the platform has any user; the zero-user window is always open)	Ask a platform administrator to create the account via 'POST /v1/users' (or flip the switch with 'PUT /v1/auth/registration' open); the first user of a fresh install can always register.
E_REGISTRY_PUSH_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_REGISTRY_PUSH_FAILED	pushing the build result to the platform registry failed (network/credentials/registry fault)	The push to registry.<base> failed: check that the fleetly-registry service is healthy and the platform registry credentials (registry.auth_file) are current, then run the build again.
E_REGISTRY_UNAVAILABLE	503	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_REGISTRY_UNAVAILABLE	registry-mode deploy preflight: the platform registry is unreachable (fail fast, no queueing)	The platform registry did not answer: check the fleetly-registry service on the manager and the registry.<base> route (Traefik); deploys fail fast until the registry responds.
E_ROLLBACK_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ROLLBACK_FAILED	rollback failed (single-layer replay of the revision)	Check the deployment record and logs to locate the replay failure; rollback can be started again.
E_ROLLBACK_NO_TARGET	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ROLLBACK_NO_TARGET	no replayable rollback target (outside the 5 most recent verified revisions/first deploy failed)	No replayable revision in history: deploy a new revision instead (default retention is 5 revisions).
E_ROUTE_PUBLISH_FAILED	503	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_ROUTE_PUBLISH_FAILED	ingress route publish failed (deploy unaffected; route alerts separately)	Check the route.publish_failed event and fleetly ingress status; once the substrate/ingress recovers, it converges automatically with the next deploy or republish.
E_RUNTIME_UNAVAILABLE	503	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_RUNTIME_UNAVAILABLE	Swarm/node substrate unreachable or operation failed	Check Docker Engine and node status and retry after the substrate recovers; the reconciler converges the observation cache automatically.
E_S3_CONFIG_CONFLICT	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_S3_CONFIG_CONFLICT	s3 settings conflict: mode=external requires endpoint/bucket/keys while mode=rustfs requires them empty (two mutually exclusive fact sources; silent overwrite is rejected)	s3.mode=external and s3.mode=rustfs are mutually exclusive: clear the external endpoint fields before switching to rustfs, or fill them all before switching to external.
E_S3_NOT_CONFIGURED	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_S3_NOT_CONFIGURED	a service declares label fleetly.s3=true but object storage is not configured (s3.mode=unset); deploy plan refuses instead of injecting empty env	Configure object storage first: run 'fleetly s3 set' (or the Console S3 settings card) to set s3.mode=external or rustfs, then deploy again.
E_S3_PUBLIC_REQUIRES_BASE_DOMAIN	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_S3_PUBLIC_REQUIRES_BASE_DOMAIN	s3.public_exposed requires a platform base domain (public subdomain s3.<base> derivation); refused in the single-node form without one	Configure base_domain (installer --base-domain) before exposing RustFS on the public subdomain s3.<base>; keep public_exposed=false for internal-only access.
E_S3_TEST_FAILED	503	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_S3_TEST_FAILED	S3 connection test failed (probe put→get→delete; the failed step and the underlying error travel in the envelope context; this is a reachable-endpoint fault, not a TCP probe)	Fix the endpoint/credentials per the failed probe step (put=auth/write, get=readback, delete=cleanup) and test again; the honest contract is: test passed = can authenticate, can write, can read back.
E_SCHEDULER_PENDING_TIMEOUT	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_SCHEDULER_PENDING_TIMEOUT	task stuck in PENDING past the deploy watchdog (placement constraints/insufficient resources/node unavailable)	Check node resources and placement constraints (whether the bound node is ready); free resources or adjust constraints and retry.
E_SECRET_NOT_FOUND	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_SECRET_NOT_FOUND	a compose-declared external secret is not in the platform secret store (deploy preflight)	Create the secret first (fleetly secrets set) with the exact declared name, then deploy again; compose secrets must declare external: true.
E_STATE_VERSION_CONFLICT	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_STATE_VERSION_CONFLICT	read-before-write optimistic concurrency conflict (object version token invalid)	The object was modified concurrently: re-read the latest state and retry with the new version token.
E_TASK_START_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TASK_START_FAILED	new task failed to start (image entrypoint/resource limits/runtime error)	Check the task logs to locate the start failure, fix it, and retry.
E_TEAM_LAST_OWNER	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TEAM_LAST_OWNER	last-team-owner guard: removing or demoting the only owner would leave the team without a responsible party	Grant the owner role to another member first (POST /v1/teams/{team_id}/members:set-role), then retry; a team always keeps at least one owner.
E_TEAM_SLUG_RESERVED	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TEAM_SLUG_RESERVED	the team slug collides with a platform-reserved component name (v0.3 naming formulas derive fleetly-<team>-* objects from the team slug; the reserved set guards the prefix families)	Pick another slug outside the reserved set (listed in the error message); slugs are lowercase word-form identifiers [a-z0-9]{2,32} and immutable once created.
E_TERMINAL_DISABLED	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TERMINAL_DISABLED	the web terminal feature is disabled (terminal.enabled=false): no exec relay is deployed and no terminal tickets are issued	Enable the feature by setting terminal.enabled: true in the control plane config and restarting fleetlyd; the exec relay duty converges the fleetly-exec service on every node automatically.
E_TOKEN_LAST_ADMIN	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TOKEN_LAST_ADMIN	last-admin guard: revoking would leave no unrevoked admin token on the platform; self-lockout rejected	This is the last unrevoked admin token: create a new admin token before revoking this one (otherwise the platform becomes unmanageable, and the bootstrap token is not reseeded on restart).
E_VOLUME_NODE_MISMATCH	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_VOLUME_NODE_MISMATCH	volume data node ≠ target deploy node (data-safety sentinel that turns the empty-volume incident into a 409)	Declare a data disposition and retry: --data-restored (rebuilt by the restore flow) or --discard (admin+confirm; the old volume becomes orphaned).
E_WEBHOOK_NAME_CONFLICT	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_WEBHOOK_NAME_CONFLICT	a webhook endpoint with the same name already exists (endpoint names are unique)	Pick another endpoint name (or delete the old endpoint first); names are the operator-facing handle used by the CLI and Console.
E_WEBHOOK_NOT_FOUND	404	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_WEBHOOK_NOT_FOUND	the webhook endpoint referenced by the operation does not exist (or was already deleted)	List the endpoints with 'fleetly notifications endpoint list' and retry with an existing name or id. Deleting an endpoint also removes its delivery ledger rows.
E_WEBHOOK_PATTERN_INVALID	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_WEBHOOK_PATTERN_INVALID	a webhook event pattern is invalid (patterns must be a non-empty list of 1..128 chars from [a-z0-9._-*]; '*' is the wildcard)	Use event-name glob patterns like "deployment.*", "cron.failed" or "*" (matches everything); see 'fleetly events watch' for the event vocabulary the patterns match against.
W_DEPLOY_INSTABILITY	0	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/W_DEPLOY_INSTABILITY	post-observe-window instability alert (one source of app degraded)	Instability detected at runtime: check app logs to assess; the platform alerts once and advises manual rollback (no escalation counter).
W_DEPLOY_NO_HEALTHCHECK	0	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/W_DEPLOY_NO_HEALTHCHECK	service declares no healthcheck, health_gate=none (health gate skipped)	Add a healthcheck to the service; without one the health gate is skipped and the deploy passes straight through.
W_ENV_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE	0	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/W_ENV_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE	platform-layer env_vars overrides same-named keys from files (three-layer merge chain)	Platform-layer env overrides same-named compose keys: the merge result follows the platform layer; check the platform env_vars.
W_PLACEMENT_STATELESS_PIN	0	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/W_PLACEMENT_STATELESS_PIN	stateless app auto-pinned because a new volume was added (data birthplace)	The stateless app was pinned because of the new volume: remove the volume declaration if free scheduling is needed.
W_ROLLBACK_IMAGE_RISK	0	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/W_ROLLBACK_IMAGE_RISK	rollback target declared by tag; its content may have changed (not an immutable digest)	The rollback target image is declared by tag and its content may have changed: confirm the image content before replaying.
